# A station lost with visiting vehicles at it (2026-10-21, CLAUDE.md "Launches" > Visiting vehicles: the station's
# loss): Tiangong broken up with a Shenzhou and a Tianzhou docked (the crew undocks in an emergency, the cargo ship
# goes with the station), a Progress turned away on its approach to ROS, a Crew Dragon's rendezvous with the ISS
# called off in its phasing orbit. Every flight's timeline follows from the Kessler event log.
#   python tools/harness/run.py --script tools/harness/scripts/station_loss.satcmd
set clouds_v2.coverage 0
wait 20
# 1. Docked: Tianzhou and Shenzhou at Tiangong.
time set 2036-11-22T00:00:00Z
launch crew craft=tianzhou event=dock lead=-86400 follow=1
wait settle
capture loss_tiangong_before
launch state
select const "Tiangong"
kessler breakup sel
wait 10
launch state
capture loss_tiangong_at
time add 240
wait settle
launch state
capture loss_tiangong_escape
# 2. On the approach: a Progress 200 m off ROS.
time set 2036-11-22T00:00:00Z
launch crew craft=progress station=russian event=hold200 lead=-60 follow=1
wait settle
select const "Russian"
kessler breakup sel
wait 10
launch state
time add 900
wait settle
launch state
capture loss_progress_turned_away
missions milestone list
# 3. Phasing: a Crew Dragon on its way to the ISS.
time set 2036-11-22T00:00:00Z
launch crew craft=crew station=international event=phasing lead=-60 follow=1
wait settle
select const "International Space Station"
kessler breakup sel
wait 10
launch state
missions milestone list
launch check
